      "staff": false,
      "text": "<@465912833352138768> Hey JoshMD! We audited the combat logs and combat engine for this air attack:\n\n**1. The 60 Bombers Claim:**\n• Database records confirm Rughzhenhaide had **0 bombers** and **7 fighters** at the time of the battle.\n• They lost 1 fighter (leaving 6). The claim of having 60 bombers was just psychological warfare in chat.\n• The fight loss happened because the combat roll RNG range was large enough that a bad roll on your side allowed a much smaller force to win the individual skirmish roll.\n\n**2. Bug Fix Deployed:**\nWhile auditing this, we discovered and fixed an issue in the casualty engine:\n• When an attacker sent a single unit type (e.g. 79 fighters) against a defender fielding multiple unit types (e.g. fighters + bombers + helicopters), the engine previously used `zip(winner_units, loser_units)` which truncated after the 1st unit type, causing secondary unit types to take 0 casualties.\n• We have rewritten the casualty calculations so that all fielded unit types are evaluated independently and suffer proportional losses regardless of force composition.\n\nThank you for reporting this!"
